# Claude Code Runtime Data - SENSITIVE FILES
# These files contain credentials, session data, and personal information

# Credentials and auth tokens (NEVER COMMIT)
**/.credentials.json
**/.claude.json
**/.claude.json.backup

# Runtime session data
**/projects/
**/todos/
**/shell-snapshots/
**/logs/
**/statsig/

# Plugin state
**/plugins/

# Per-account runtime markers (cleanup timestamps etc.) - regenerated, never source
**/.last-cleanup

# Account settings.json are Nix build output (regenerated by home-manager switch)
# and embed /nix/store hashes that churn on every toolchain bump, so they stay
# ignored (the account paths are listed in the parent .gitignore). Only the
# web-session file (.claude/settings.json) is tracked.
!.claude/settings.json
!**/mcp.json
# The per-account CLAUDE.md (.claude-max / .claude-pro / .claude-work) are Nix build
# output - regenerated from modules/programs/claude-code/_hm/claude-code-user-memory-template.md
# on every `home-manager switch` - so they MUST stay ignored (the parent .gitignore
# ignores claude-runtime/.claude-*/CLAUDE.md). Editing them by hand is pointless; edit
# the template instead. Only the hand-maintained web-session pointer is tracked:
!.claude/CLAUDE.md

# Allow directory structure
!**/agents/
!**/commands/